{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CeB2dimZjD8ByGfVQirWn1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation based on the research context provided. Let me analyze the project carefully.\n\nKey information:\n- Project: symb_invariant_consensus (SICA - Symbolic Invariant Consensus Aggregation)\n- Core method: Extract FOL constraints from LLM reasoning traces, use weighted partial MAX-SAT to find globally consistent answer\n- Key metric: C0 (multi-candidate rate) determines when SICA helps\n- Current data: sica_d012_14b shows +3.3pp gap (SICA 73.3% vs SC 70.0%) on 60 questions, p=0.2261 (not significant)\n\n\n- FOLIO shows stronger results at +6.7pp (80.0% vs 73.3%), while ProofWriter shows no improvement\n- The expanded experiment with 804 questions is currently running, targeting EMNLP 2026 Main with an ARR deadline of May 25\n\nI need to establish tier definitions around the SICA-SC performance gap, statistical significance, cross-family validation through C0 metrics, constraint ablation effectiveness, and tiebreak handling to properly evaluate the Dream simulation outcomes.\n\nLooking at the win rate scenarios: best case would have the expanded results confirm the gap with statistical significance and cross-family validation showing consistent C0 patterns across Mistral and LLaMA, validating all three core claims. The median scenario shows a smaller but still positive gap that might only reach significance on FOLIO, requiring me to reframe the contribution around characterizing the operating regime rather than claiming raw accuracy improvements. Worst case would see the gap disappear or become insignificant on the expanded dataset, triggering the contingency plan and forcing a reframing toward analysis rather than empirical gains.\n\nNow I'm defining the specific metrics I need to track: the combined gap in percentage points, the FOLIO-specific gap, statistical significance via bootstrap or McNemar test, whether the C0 pattern replicates across model families, the tiebreak win rate, and the constraint ablation delta showing MaxSAT outperforming count-only baselines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12569,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12569},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf02ff40-6ce9-42a2-bb4b-5ee2c4a82315","uuid":"69e8ab8a-91a5-4d39-85d9-89d2de68b9d1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CeB2dimZjD8ByGfVQirWn1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"exp-001 confirms d012 signal at scale with significance; cross-family C0 pattern replicates cleanly; MaxSAT ablation shows clear satisfiability value\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"FOLIO gap ≥+5pp persists at 204-question scale with p<0.05\"\n      - \"Combined (PW+FOLIO) gap ≥+2pp with p<0.10\"\n      - \"Cross-family (Mistral/LLaMA) C0>25% and SICA≥SC on both\"\n      - \"MaxSAT > count-only by ≥2pp on tie-subset\"\n      - \"DeepSeek-R1 confirms C0<5% (second reasoning model degeneration)\"\n      - \"7B C0 > 14B C0 > 72B C0 monotonic trend holds\"\n    number_ranges:\n      folio_gap_pp: [5.0, 8.5]\n      combined_gap_pp: [2.0, 4.5]\n      bootstrap_p_folio: [0.01, 0.05]\n      bootstrap_p_combined: [0.05, 0.10]\n      c0_14b_expanded: [0.40, 0.60]\n      c0_mistral_7b: [0.30, 0.55]\n      c0_llama_8b: [0.30, 0.55]\n      c0_deepseek_r1: [0.00, 0.05]\n      tiebreak_win_rate: [0.70, 0.85]\n      maxsat_vs_countonly_delta_pp: [2.0, 5.0]\n      c0_7b: [0.55, 0.75]\n      c0_72b: [0.15, 0.35]\n    narrative_direction: \"All 3 claims stand as-is. Story: SICA provides principled tiebreaking (+5-8pp on FOLIO), C0 is a continuous predictor validated across 3 families + 2 reasoning architectures, MaxSAT satisfiability checking is essential (not over-engineering). Hero figure shows clean C0-vs-gap scatter with monotonic trend. Title stays as-is. Target: EMNLP Main acceptance.\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"FOLIO gain real but smaller at scale; ProofWriter dilutes combined significance; cross-family C0 pattern holds directionally but gains are noisy; MaxSAT marginal over counting\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"FOLIO gap +3-5pp, p in 0.05-0.15 range (trending but not clean)\"\n      - \"Combined gap +1-2pp, p>0.15 (not significant)\"\n      - \"Cross-family C0>20% confirmed but SICA-SC gap inconsistent across families (one shows gain, one flat)\"\n      - \"MaxSAT ≥ count-only but delta <2pp (marginal)\"\n      - \"C0 scaling trend noisy (7B>14B holds but 72B not clearly below 14B)\"\n      - \"Tiebreak win rate 60-70% (above random but not dominant)\"\n    number_ranges:\n      folio_gap_pp: [3.0, 5.0]\n      combined_gap_pp: [0.5, 2.0]\n      bootstrap_p_folio: [0.05, 0.15]\n      bootstrap_p_combined: [0.15, 0.30]\n      c0_14b_expanded: [0.35, 0.50]\n      c0_mistral_7b: [0.20, 0.40]\n      c0_llama_8b: [0.20, 0.40]\n      c0_deepseek_r1: [0.00, 0.08]\n      tiebreak_win_rate: [0.60, 0.72]\n      maxsat_vs_countonly_delta_pp: [0.5, 2.0]\n      c0_7b: [0.45, 0.60]\n      c0_72b: [0.25, 0.45]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 1 weakens: reframe from 'accuracy improvement' to 'principled interpretable tiebreaking with positive trend on formal-logic domains.' Claim 2 becomes the lead — operating regime characterization is the primary contribution, validated by C0 pattern across families (even if per-family gains are noisy). Claim 3 downgrades from 'continuous predictor' to 'binary diagnostic' (C0>20% = try SICA, C0<5% = skip). MaxSAT framed as 'provides interpretability + marginal gains' not 'essential for accuracy.' Paper restructured: §1-2 motivate operating regime question, §3-4 present C0 framework + validation, §5 shows FOLIO as strongest evidence. Title shifts to: 'When Does Symbolic Consensus Help?' (drop 'Characterizing Operating Regime'). Target: EMNLP Main (25-30%) / Findings (55-65%).\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Expanded results show SICA≈SC overall; FOLIO gain shrinks to noise at scale; D023 contingency triggered — must pivot to analysis paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"FOLIO gap ≤+2pp at 204-question scale, p>0.20\"\n      - \"Combined gap ≤+0.5pp (effectively zero)\"\n      - \"Cross-family C0 pattern holds (C0>20% for instruction models) BUT high C0 does not reliably translate to SICA>SC\"\n      - \"MaxSAT ≈ count-only (no satisfiability value)\"\n      - \"Tiebreak win rate 50-60% (barely above random on expanded set)\"\n      - \"Core failure: constraint extraction quality insufficient to consistently beat voting even when traces diverge\"\n    number_ranges:\n      folio_gap_pp: [-1.0, 2.0]\n      combined_gap_pp: [-1.0, 0.5]\n      bootstrap_p_folio: [0.20, 0.50]\n      bootstrap_p_combined: [0.35, 0.60]\n      c0_14b_expanded: [0.30, 0.50]\n      c0_mistral_7b: [0.15, 0.40]\n      c0_llama_8b: [0.15, 0.40]\n      c0_deepseek_r1: [0.00, 0.08]\n      tiebreak_win_rate: [0.45, 0.60]\n      maxsat_vs_countonly_delta_pp: [-1.0, 0.5]\n      c0_7b: [0.40, 0.65]\n      c0_72b: [0.20, 0.45]\n    narrative_direction: \"D023 activated. All 3 original claims abandoned as accuracy claims. Paper pivots to: 'Why Doesn't Symbolic Consensus Improve LLM Reasoning? A Diagnostic Study.' New contribution structure: (1) C0 as a reliable zero-cost indicator of output diversity across model families — characterizes WHEN models disagree, not IF symbolic methods help; (2) Negative result on constraint-based aggregation — identifies failure modes (extraction noise, shallow constraints that don't capture deep reasoning errors); (3) Taxonomy of reasoning model vs instruction model behavior under sampling — reasoning models are structurally self-consistent regardless of temperature/K. Supplement with constraint-quality-vs-delta correlation analysis (CPU-only). Frame QwQ/DeepSeek convergence as novel finding about reasoning model internals. Target: EMNLP Findings (50-60%) with AAAI 2027 Main as fallback if reviewers want more models.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12569,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12569},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_managem